{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794351392,"nonce":"Guqd3qiYfTjJmoRgfX/oJMDwp8E=","message":"**Reproducer and counts: the key backlog is the event-loop thread blocking in `get_current_texture()`.**\n\nReproducer (laptop, GPU, Release builds): a window with text inputs under a virtual KWin with the `de` layout; 43 keys injected 120 ms apart through `org_kde_kwin_fake_input`; the app's own `WAYLAND_DEBUG` trace shows when each key reaches it and when the next `wl_surface.commit` follows. Script and injector: https://github.com/FreeSynergy/fs-release/tree/q1b-typing-test/scripts/typing-test (`TT_PHASE=latency TT_CLICK_REL=220,177 scripts/typing-test.sh \u003cbinary\u003e`; `TT_SAMPLE=1` also samples the main thread's wait channel every 50 ms). A run counts as a stall if a key waits more than 500 ms for the next commit, or 3 or more keys injected 120 ms apart reach the app within 40 ms of each other.\n\nRuns per variant, runs with a gap \u003e 500 ms / runs with any stall (two runs at a time on the machine):\n\n| build | runs | gap \u003e 500 ms | any stall |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| fs-components example `form`, old pin (blinc-app-fix) | 20 | 13 | 20 |\n| same, tag fs-blinc-1 | 20 | 16 | 20 |\n| same, tag fs-blinc-2 | 20 | 9 | 19 |\n| fs-maps, old pin | 20 | 13 | 20 |\n| fs-maps, fs-blinc-1 | 20 | 12 | 19 |\n| fs-maps, fs-blinc-2 | 20 | 11 | 14 |\n\nFurther runs with `form` on fs-blinc-2, 10 each: `BLINC_KEEP_ALIVE=1` 4 with a gap \u003e 500 ms, `BLINC_KEEP_ALIVE=0` 9, `BLINC_PRESENT_MODE=mailbox` 2, `immediate` 3; KWin nested in the running compositor (real frame callbacks, nothing injected into the host session) 6, any stall in 10 of 10. A Qt program (kcalc) in the same virtual KWin with the same injector: 0 of 43 keys bundled, so injection and KWin's delivery are fine. Medians stay at 5 to 7 ms; the gaps are about 1.05 s each.\n\nWhere it waits: the main thread sits in `drm_syncobj_array_wait_timeout` (51 % of the samples with keep-alive on, 63 % with it off, 97 % nested; up to 4 s in a row) and in `ep_poll` otherwise. The render path runs on the winit loop thread and calls `surf.get_current_texture()` there (`crates/blinc_app/src/windowed/event_loop/frame.rs:220`, tag fs-blinc-2; second path `windowed/event_loop.rs:460`). While that acquire waits for a free swapchain image (up to the 1 s timeout) nobody reads the Wayland socket, so the keys queue up and arrive together. This is the starvation the comments in `windowed/window.rs:186`, `lifecycle.rs:154` and `frame.rs:81` describe; the keep-alive makes it rarer but does not remove it, and Mailbox lessens it without removing it either.\n\nNot a fix, a direction: acquire and present off the event-loop thread (events handled at once, state changed, drawing on its own thread with a bounded wait), with Mailbox and three or more images as an intermediate step. That changes the frame loop, so nothing is proposed as a patch here.","files":null}]}